diff --git a/scripts/acceptance/check-create-recovery/README.md b/scripts/acceptance/check-create-recovery/README.md
index 30ef1549..7e9a8cc6 100644
--- a/scripts/acceptance/check-create-recovery/README.md
+++ b/scripts/acceptance/check-create-recovery/README.md
@@ -26,6 +26,10 @@ Explicit `--charged-witness` adds one real unrelated reservation, held before Cr
 
 Workflow budget is 600 seconds, cleanup 180 seconds. Wrapper adds 120 seconds preparation and enforces one 900-second driver budget. Forced or uncertain termination fails. The source-bound shared cgroup observer follows only the driver's exact team-instance pointer. Measurement provenance is separate from recovery success. An image-free retained marker may yield explicit identity/label diagnostics in the frozen observer; do not present those as runnable-check samples or silently discard them.
 
+Before each single consented checks POST, the adapter waits up to 30 seconds, also bounded by the remaining 600-second workflow budget, for fresh host/execution observations and enough capacity for the complete private ledger plus the prospective 1 GiB/1,000 mCPU check. Existing 25%/minimum 2 GiB headroom, 6 GiB Create floor and 1 GiB working reserve remain unchanged. The CPU utilization ceiling follows `100 - policy.headroomPercent` (75% with this fixture's required policy). These read-only observations are advisory: installed admission still decides after the POST, and a later refusal never causes resubmission. Public readiness diagnostics include a canonical parsed-ledger hash and counts, not its private records; that hash is explicitly distinct from a raw ledger-file hash.
+
+After submission, all historical/target/optional-witness gate waits observe the exact check alongside the real proxy gate. A terminal check before gate capture fails promptly with `check-terminal-before-create-gate`, retaining its revision/reason and a separately timestamped current resource/policy observation (or its unavailable error). Gate capture is checked again after the check GET so a genuine lost-ACK gate can win the race with the resulting unknown receipt. Acknowledgement still comes from the actual matching proxy gate, including exact project/check labels and daemon 201/immutable identity for after-response gates. Neither a terminal receipt nor a resource sample fabricates a daemon acknowledgement. Gate waits retain the 120-second bound and the remaining overall workflow deadline.
+
 Exact charge/release proof comes from the complete private shared ledger. The baseline 4df owner's public scheduler summary is a process-local cache and can miss a team child's changes. Default mode preserves it only as diagnostic evidence. For a matching product containing the CLOUD-034 correction, add `--require-public-reservations`: each quiescent charged/released checkpoint requires the current owner's public `ready` observation to be at most 5 seconds old and match the complete ledger's count/memory/CPU. Explicit `unavailable` responses retry only that GET within a 10-second checkpoint budget, then fail; absent/legacy/malformed/stale/incorrect ready totals fail. This visibility assertion never replaces exact allocation ownership, absence/fence or release proof. No installed CLOUD-034 visibility result is claimed by controlled tests.
 
 Credentials remain in memory/fresh private fixture. Bounded phase/final JSON rejects known credential literals; no raw Create body or auth header is exported. Screenshots and proposed public artifacts require later secret review. Publication is not part of preparation.
